 <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:49:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PM: domains: Fix the cached power-down state index being a
 bool
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

genpd_governor_data::cached_power_down_state_idx has been declared bool
since it was introduced in commit e94999688e3a ("PM / Domains: Add genpd
governor for CPUs"), while every value assigned to and read from it is a
state index of type unsigned int:

	gd->cached_power_down_state_idx = genpd->state_idx;
	...
	genpd->state_idx = gd->cached_power_down_state_idx;

Any index above 1 is therefore stored as 1. A genpd with three or more
idle states can compute the correct deepest index once, on the single
uncached pass, and then loses it forever: every later call takes the
cached path and hands the governor a 1. cpu_power_down_ok() starts its
search at genpd->state_idx and only ever walks downwards, so from that
point on no state deeper than index 1 can be selected again.

Measured on an msm8953 phone, whose CPU cluster domains have three idle
states (retention, GDHS, power collapse) and whose system domain sits
above them. Over 60 s of display-off idle before the fix, the deepest
cluster state was entered 0 times out of 22 thousand domain idle entries,
with a rejected count of 0 - it was never refused, it was never offered.
A trace of the governor showed 73% of those decisions had a next-wakeup
estimate beyond the state's residency plus power-off latency, and every
single one of them started its search at index 1. After the fix the same
60 s enters it 14516 times for 67 s of residency, and the system-level
domain above the clusters, which can only power off once every child is
in its deepest state, goes from 0 to 3531 power-offs.

Residency counters are not by themselves a power saving, so the effect
was also measured at the battery. With the panel genuinely off and the
charger's USB input suspended so the fuel gauge reports real discharge,
interleaved A/B legs of 200 samples each taken after a 300 s settle give
130.5 mA unfixed against 119.0 mA fixed, the two arms not overlapping:
about 9% of the idle draw of the entire phone.

That figure is conditional on the display being off, and worth stating
because it caught me out. With the panel refreshing at 65 Hz the same
comparison reverses sign, and correctly so - the idle windows never grow
long enough for the deepest state to repay its entry cost. The fix makes
a deeper state reachable; whether reaching it pays depends, as it should,
on how long the domain gets to stay there.

Fixes: e94999688e3a ("PM / Domains: Add genpd governor for CPUs")
Signed-off-by: Lajosházi, László Gergely <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
---

Tool disclosure, per Documentation/process/generated-content.rst:

This patch was produced with the assistance of Claude (claude-opus-5) driven
from Claude Code, working under my direction on a mainline port of the
Fairphone 3 (sdm632/msm8953). The assistant was asked why the CPU cluster
power domain never selected its deepest idle state; it wrote the temporary
trace_printk instrumentation described in the commit message, ran the three
instrumented boots on the device, read the resulting traces, located the
field, and drafted this patch and its message. I reviewed the change and the
measurements.

The tool-affected portion is the whole of this patch, which is a one-word
type change, and all of the commit message.

Testing: built and booted on a Fairphone 3 (sdm632, four cpu domains per
cluster, three cluster idle states, a system domain above them). Measured
with the genpd debugfs idle_states counters over 60 s of display-off idle,
before and after, with no other difference between the two kernels. The
figures in the commit message are those two runs. scripts/checkpatch.pl
--strict is clean; the patch applies to torvalds master as of 2026-08-14.

Recipients from scripts/get_maintainer.pl: Rafael J. Wysocki, Ulf Hansson,
Daniel Lezcano, linux-pm, linux-kernel.
 include/linux/pm_domain.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/pm_domain.h b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
index b299dc0128d6..9b1aa61692d3 100644
--- a/include/linux/pm_domain.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@ struct genpd_governor_data {
 	ktime_t last_enter;
 	bool reflect_residency;
 	bool cached_power_down_ok;
-	bool cached_power_down_state_idx;
+	unsigned int cached_power_down_state_idx;
 };
 
 struct genpd_power_state {

